47|0@2007scape^1438955247#cturilb:EZScape$:Devil's Advocate here. As much as I know people in this game are truely appreciative to nice higher level people, there will always be the players to come along to ruin it. When F2P came out I would pick a random day and take 1m out of my bank to give 10 noobs 100k and teach them how to play. Now when I go to a F2P world just to give another account a bond I get spam traded asking for free stuff and called names if I don't comply. The greed some people have in this game leads to a lot of scamming, and screwing other people over for personal gain. People involved with this either become attuned to this lifestyle over other MMORPGs and the victims are actually scarred with trust issues. As far as what I've seen this is more the case than what's in the OP, and I wish it was different. As for the noobs I would help out they would either come to me for more money, quit, or lose it to another player/own stupidity so I stopped.
